#testresult/e0f0ae06db70326e","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793916134000,"stop":1793916381440,"duration":247440}},{"uid":"821c845eccb6a87d","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/8/#testresult/821c845eccb6a87d","status":"failed","statusDetails":"failed to connect to the broker at 10.208.13.244:50221: rpc error: code = Unavailable desc = connection error: desc = \"transport: Error while dialing: dial tcp 10.208.13.244:50221: connect: no route to host\"\n\nClaude's conclusion:\n### Root cause\n\nThe suite failed in `Init()` itself, 4 seconds after Adam/image-server startup, trying to establish the harness's very first gRPC connection to the Proxmox/VM-provisioning **broker** at `10.208.13.244:50221` — before any EVE device, SDN VM, or app was ever created (`evetest status` confirms \"No EVE devices found\", and `evetest sdn status` reports \"SDN client is not initialized\"). The error (`no route to host`) is an immediate network-layer rejection, not a stall, indicating the broker host/VM was unreachable from the very start of the run rather than becoming unresponsive due to anything EVE-side.\n\nThis does **not** share a root cause with anything else in this run (no other suite has failed yet) and it's a different failure mode from the only prior occurrence of this exact endpoint, `10.208.13.244:50221`, in the ledger (2026-11-03, run #6): there, the broker connection worked fine initially and only died *mid-run* (first as `i/o timeout`, later degrading to `network is unreachable`) as a downstream consequence of an `edge-dev` qemu guest wedging in host-kernel state `D` (`kvm_async_pf_task_wait_schedule`). Tonight's failure instead happens pre-anything, on the first dial attempt, with no device or guest involved — so it's not a repeat of that cascade, just a coincidentally identical IP (likely a reused DHCP lease on the Proxmox broker VM). I found no prior ledger entry matching this \"broker unreachable at harness Init before any device exists\" signature, so this looks like a new infrastructure-level outage (Proxmox broker host/VM down or unreachable at the network level), not a known/recurring issue and not a pillar/EVE code defect. No PR diff was provided to assess code relatedness.","time":{"start":1793841399000,"stop":1793841468620,"duration":69620}},{"uid":"c35179d7dd068cb0","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/7/#testresult/c35179d7dd068cb0","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793744477000,"stop":1793744656350,"duration":179350}},{"uid":"fec853ce71990505","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/6/#testresult/fec853ce71990505","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793661915000,"stop":1793662227560,"duration":312560}},{"uid":"7d8fba632ae6c9a4","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/5/#testresult/7d8fba632ae6c9a4","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793576162000,"stop":1793576331920,"duration":169920}},{"uid":"96b3b616b5b82e94","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/4/#testresult/96b3b616b5b82e94","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793491883000,"stop":1793492071900,"duration":188900}}]},"tags":[]},"source":"ed39742aeaf55de2.json","parameterValues":[]}